keywork — third-party attributions

keywork independently implements ideas from, and may adapt code from, the projects
below. "Adaptations" lists code actually copied or closely derived, recorded by the
backlog task that introduced it. Design/format influences without copied code carry
no MIT obligation and are credited in docs/influencers/.

---

Pi (https://github.com/earendil-works/pi-mono, published as @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent)
Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner
Licensed under the MIT License (full text below).

Adaptations:
- B1/B4-B6/B8 (packages/engine/src/session/entries.ts, store.ts): session entry
  vocabulary and JSONL tree semantics adapted from Pi's session-manager, format
  version 3 — the entry union (message / compaction / branch_summary / label /
  session_info / custom / custom_message / thinking_level_change / model_change,
  each with id/parentId/timestamp), leaf-pointer branching, compaction-aware
  context assembly, tree read API, and branched-session cloning with a
  parentSession header reference. Message payloads inside entries are keywork's
  own message shape, not Pi's.
- B7 (packages/engine/src/session/compaction.ts): compaction algorithm adapted
  from Pi's documented design (docs/compaction.md in the published package) —
  reserve-token trigger, keep-recent backward cut walk with message-boundary cut
  points (never at tool results), iterative structured summaries that fold the
  previous summary, cumulative read/modified file tracking in compaction details,
  and serialized-conversation summarization input with tool-result truncation.

